Tile Images
  Every tile image this app ships is generated with OpenAI image models.
  Per OpenAI's Terms of Service, generated content is owned by the requester.
  They carry no license beyond the Apache License above: no attribution
  requirement, no non-commercial restriction, nothing to replace before
  distribution.

  No ARASAAC pictogram, and no other third-party artwork, ships in this
  product, and none is present anywhere in the current source tree.

  Git history is the exception, and it matters if you build from an old
  commit. Earlier versions bundled 493 ARASAAC pictograms under
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. They were deleted in commit c203207 (July 2026) and
  replaced with generated art, but deleting a file does not remove it from
  history: every clone of this repository still contains those blobs, and
  any checkout of a commit before c203207 will put them back on disk.

  Those files remain under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and the Apache License above does
  not extend to them. If you build, distribute, or reuse artwork from a tree
  that predates c203207, you take on ARASAAC's terms for that artwork —
  attribution, non-commercial use, and share-alike — regardless of what
  LICENSE says at the root. Build from a commit at or after c203207 and
  none of that applies.

  "ARASAAC" also survives in the current source as a description of a drawing
  style inside a generation prompt (Resources/image_styles.json). A style is
  not a licensable asset, and no ARASAAC file remains in the working tree.

  Art a caregiver generates on their own device with their own OpenAI key
  belongs to them on the same terms, and this project asserts no license
  over it. Exports say so: an .obz reports Apache-2.0 for bundled art and
  attributes caregiver-generated art to its author without claiming a
  license on their behalf.

Wordbank Data
  tools/data/wordbank/english_american_ws_aoa.csv is derived from Wordbank
  (Stanford University), licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It is the English
  (American) Words & Sentences slice of Wordbank's age-of-acquisition table,
  Redivis dataset datapages.wordbank v3.4 (doi:10.57761/t38b-5y26), reduced
  to five columns. It is a development tool's input and does not ship in the
  app.

  Frank, M. C., Braginsky, M., Yurovsky, D., & Marchman, V. A. (2017).
  Wordbank: An open repository for developmental vocabulary data. Journal of
  Child Language, 44(3), 677–694.

  Wordbank's data was collected with the MacArthur-Bates Communicative
  Development Inventories, which are copyrighted by the CDI Advisory Board
  and are not reproduced here.
